From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Caboose <caboose@invalid>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 43/43] Hold the phone's own device-loss replies for a paused
 application

A phone whose app is closing reports VK_ERROR_DEVICE_LOST in its replies
before the executor's streams end, so a paused application (CABOOSE_GPU_ON_LOSS
resolved to pause) saw the loss at once. Every VkResult the encoder returns
passes through caboose::completion::heldLoss
(../bounded-memory/completion_feed.h): a device loss is held while the
executor leaves within the departure grace and reported once a new executor
is there, and reported after the grace when the executor stays.

diff --git a/src/gfxstream/guest/vulkan_enc/autogenerated/VkEncoder.cpp b/src/gfxstream/guest/vulkan_enc/autogenerated/VkEncoder.cpp
index 592f4c2..a674223 100644
--- a/src/gfxstream/guest/vulkan_enc/autogenerated/VkEncoder.cpp
+++ b/src/gfxstream/guest/vulkan_enc/autogenerated/VkEncoder.cpp
@@ -493,7 +493,7 @@ VkResult VkEncoder::vkCreateInstance(const VkInstanceCreateInfo* pCreateInfo,
         stream->clearPool();
     }
     if (!queueSubmitWithCommandsEnabled && doLock) this->unlock();
-    return vkCreateInstance_VkResult_return;
+    return caboose::completion::heldLoss(vkCreateInstance_VkResult_return);
 }
 
